+### `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA` (ROCm gfx1200 / gfx1201; default: `0`)
+
+Multi-row EXL3 GEMV (2-8 rows, e.g. a speculative verify) on the gfx12 WMMA units: each 16x16
+trellis tile is decoded once and one `v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16` takes all rows, instead of one
+fdot2 chain per row. Covers integer bitrates in the single-matrix GEMV and the unweighted
+single-token multi-matrix GEMV; everything else keeps the fdot2 kernels. Devices other than
+gfx1200 / gfx1201 (gfx11 included) also keep them whatever the setting: eligibility is checked per
+device at runtime. Results match the fdot2 path to fp32 rounding, not bit for bit. Read on every
+call, unlike most C++-side variables, so tests can toggle it.
+
+### `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA_U` (default: `4`)
+
+k-tiles decoded per WMMA batch in the `EXL3_GEMV_WMMA` kernel: `1`, `2` or `4`.
+
 ### `EXL3_INT8_GEMV` (default: `2`)
 
 Fused int8-activation GEMV for tensors quantized with the mul1 codebook: one cooperative launch
